Q: how to use insert method with select method in one query in codeigniter? A: <p><strong>Hope this will help you :</strong></p>

<p><em>You can do it by  selecting the  columns to be inserted first</em></p>

<pre><code>/*change your table name here*/
$table = 'users';

/*change your column column_name1 , column_name2 with your table column*/
$sql = 'INSERT into '.$table.' (column_name1, column_name2) 
        SELECT column_name1, column_name2 FROM '.$table;

$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;query($sql);
</code></pre>

<p>Or you can use query builder like this :</p>

<pre><code>/*change your table name here*/
$table = 'users';

$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('column_name1, column_name2');
$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get($table);
if ($query-&gt;num_rows() &gt; 0)
{
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;insert($table, $query-&gt;row());
    /*for multiple rows use insert_batch()*/
}
</code></pre>
